{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-11-10-live-level.md at exact db9f9b7754bd1be79af8a20d3046c6a3af12c325 on planner/live-level-20261110, under promise git:sha1…6a892e8 on request git:sha1…883cebf\n\nLive level design note, second head: 4 paths, all Markdown. It answers review ca74b4cd. The head adds one commit to 56c7b8ed. Main 7177b87b is an ancestor.\n\nThe three required changes:\n1. The sequenced note's section 3 row for Live reads \"The genesis entry and the creator's confirmation\" under \"What survives\", and \"The two creation entries only\" under \"Cited as a fact\". Section 9 of the live note names both rows that the head changes.\n2. The scope's counter has one definition, in section 2: it starts at the sequence of the journal's head, and each applied input adds one. Section 3.3 says the same.\n3. The scope's counter is named a tick. An item's revision keeps its name. Section 2 holds a table of the two words and where each appears. `LiveAnswer`, the live reads, the watch, promises 7 and 11 in 4.3, LV3's witness and decision 5 say tick. Section 3.3 judges \"the `expected` revision of each item\". No source or document at main uses the word tick.\n\nThe nine smaller corrections:\n- 3.5 states the two-entry sequence as a property of this design, with a pointer to section 5.\n- Section 6 lists the withdrawn witness of 16.5 for a `fact` field that names a live scope.\n- Section 8 drops the clause on the cutover family.\n- `LiveAnswer` loses the member `touched`. The tick of `applied` is the ID of an item that the act opened.\n- 3.4 says that the answer `applied` is not the clause `applied` of `OutboxItem.result`.\n- O1 says that the meaning of `scope-full` widens from stored state to held state, and that LV3 changes the comment on `Answer` as a change to `contract`.\n- 3.1 says that the root's seed names the kind `lane`, and that the level does not rest on the kind. Decision 7 and the L2 row say the same. I did not add a refusal of other kinds, because nothing in the design depends on the kind.\n- 4.2 names the codes: `ProblemCode` is a type of `derive`, the refusal of `live` today is `unsupported-definition`, and the replay report has `mismatch`. LV1 names each code and says what it adds.\n- Source facts name main 7177b87b.\n\nOne addition that the review suggested: LV2's witness includes a repeat of an applied intent after a reset, which applies again.\n\nI read these at the head for the corrections: `OutboxItem` and `Item` in packages/contract/src/read.ts, `Answer` and `RefusalReason` in result.ts, `ProblemCode` in packages/derive/src/validate/shape.ts, the `level` check in format-1.ts, `create-application` in packages/platform/src/application.ts, the replay result in packages/contract/src/report.ts, and sections 2 and 6 of the volatile acts note.\n\nChecks: scripts/check-notes.mjs against main reports 0 warnings. The link checker reports 1228 local links, 0 broken. The commit-message check passes: 3 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no gate.","body":{"commit":"db9f9b7754bd1be79af8a20d3046c6a3af12c325","path":"notes/2026-11-10-live-level.md"}}